  "question": {
    "text": "Adsorption of gas on a surface follows Freundlich adsorption isotherm.&nbsp;The plot of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac></math> versus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math> gives a straight line with slope equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, then:<br /><br />(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac></math> is the mass of the gas adsorbed per gram of adsorbent)"
